---
import ArticleLayout from '../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import ModelSpecs from '../../components/brands/ModelSpecs.astro';
import { getModelSpecs } from '../../data/model-specs';

const models = getModelSpecs('Champion');
const toc = [
  { id: 'scope', label: 'Scope of this guide' },
  { id: 'model-data', label: '201222 model data' },
  { id: 'system-bundle', label: 'Included system equipment' },
  { id: 'quote-checklist', label: 'Quote checklist' },
];
---
<ArticleLayout
  title="Champion 201222 Standby Generator: Verified Model Data"
  description="Source-linked information for Champion’s 201222 aXis standby system: fuel-specific output, published fuel use, sound caveat, included transfer switch, and separate warranty terms."
  category="Brands" categoryHref="/brands/" updated="2026-10-04" verified="2026-10-04" readingTime="6 min read" toc={toc}
  takeaways={[
    'The Champion 201222 system is rated 22 kW on LP and 19.8 kW on natural gas.',
    'The manufacturer describes the 201222 as including a 200 A aXis ATS; load-management modules are sold separately.',
    'The manufacturer states different warranty durations for the generator and ATS; verify current terms for the exact purchase.',
  ]}
  sources={[
    { label: 'Champion 201222 product page and specifications', href: 'https://www.championpowerequipment.com/product/201222-22-kw-whole-house-home-standby-generator-and-200a-switch-with-axis-technology/', type: 'Manufacturer', verified: '2026-10-04' },
  ]}
  related={[
    { href: '/brands/generac/', title: 'Generac model data', description: 'Exact model sources for 22 kW and 26 kW cellular standby units.', category: 'Brands' },
    { href: '/brands/briggs-stratton/', title: 'Briggs & Stratton model data', description: 'Published output, warranty, sound, and MSRP for model 040786.', category: 'Brands' },
    { href: '/comparisons/standby-vs-portable/', title: 'Standby vs. portable', description: 'Compare operating and installation tradeoffs.', category: 'Comparisons' },
  ]}
>
  <section id="scope">
    <h2>Scope of this guide</h2>
    <p>This page covers the exact Champion model <strong>201222</strong>, not every Champion standby product or a brand-wide price range. Manufacturer specifications and product descriptions were checked October 4, 2026. Published data is not an independent test or a site-specific recommendation.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="model-data">
    <h2>201222 model data</h2>
    <ModelSpecs models={models} label="Champion 201222 manufacturer specifications checked October 4, 2026" />
    <p class="mt-4">Champion describes its 67 dB(A) sound figure as approximate and says it is measured at 23 feet (7 m); the product page does not state the test load and cautions that the figure does not account for the installation site. Do not rank it directly against figures with different or undisclosed conditions.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="system-bundle">
    <h2>Included system equipment and warranty scope</h2>
    <p>The Champion product page identifies 201222 as a system including the 22 kW generator and a 200 A aXis automatic transfer switch. It says aXis load-management modules are sold separately. The product page also lists a <strong>10-year limited warranty for the generator</strong> and a separate <strong>2-year limited warranty for the ATS</strong>. Confirm the current warranty terms, conditions, exclusions, registration, and local servicing arrangement in the actual purchase documents.</p>
    <p>The manufacturer describes this system as “whole house,” but that label does not mean every large home appliance can run simultaneously. Capacity depends on fuel, selected loads, starts, transfer equipment, and the home-specific design. Start with a <a href="/sizing/what-size-generator-do-i-need/">load-based assessment</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="quote-checklist">
    <h2>Questions for a written proposal</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Is the exact generator model 201222, and is the included switch model/rating shown?</li>
      <li>Which aXis load-management devices are included, if any, and which high-demand circuits are excluded?</li>
      <li>Are fuel supply, electrical wiring, site preparation, permits, inspections, startup, and commissioning included?</li>
      <li>Does the local installer service Champion standby systems and handle warranty calls in this area?</li>
      <li>Which warranty applies to the generator versus the ATS, and what terms/exclusions appear in the contract?</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Do not infer comparative “value” from a brand or model label. Compare complete quotes with matching fuel, switch, load-management, and installation scope.</p>
  </section>
</ArticleLayout>
